cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite as below."
title: "Kill-Test v6 Universality — Extension of the EFC vs ΛCDM Kill-Test to the Full SPARC 175 Sample"
abstract: >-
  Extension of the EFC vs ΛCDM Kill-Test v6 (probe-2) to all 175 galaxies
  in the SPARC database. On 171 successfully fitted galaxies, single-
  component Energy-Flow Cosmology wins 60.2% against an NFW reference
  (42.1% EFC_decisive). Median ΔAIC = +6.21 (favours EFC; convention
  AIC_NFW − AIC_EFC). Mann-Whitney test between FLOW and LATENT regimes
  gives p ≈ 0. Spearman ρ(ΔAIC, v_max) = 0.11 (p = 0.15) rules out
  mass-scale selection bias. DDO 154 reproduces at ΔAIC = +125.2
  (sign-convention verified). Universality verdict: CONFIRMED at the
  single-component level — the cherry-picking objection against the
  5-galaxy probe-2 result is refuted.
